cture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan suicide bombing targets police facility in Kohat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06f51024175bc3a7f130848e66af61d29ef86dd226c1c986d4b49fbcaf02b133</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432--8b09a06dd711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A police official said the explosion killed at least 16 people, injuring many more. The attacker targeted a police facility and damaged a mosque at the site. The president blamed the attack on the TTP Pakistani Taliban.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germans have soured on Chancellor Merz — can they trade him?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d4f5a38c2600fd52e687a522ac2e8bc5549b54a7efbf7393c6e933a556ee32c</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germans-have-soured-on-chancellor-merz-can-they-trade-him/a-79313623--0917e11a1245.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germans-have-soured-on-chancellor-merz-can-they-trade-him/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'No compromises': Far-right AfD has few potential partners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3cd7d67d449ddf3c4f29ea5a0f5505b4dd6413fe220980d43cc6bc1a8b8d34b</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-compromises-far-right-afd-has-few-potential-partners/a-79326208--c5bd1a26f736.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-compromises-far-right-afd-has-few-potential-partners/a-79326208?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party is riding high after its latest electoral triumph in Saxony-Anhalt. But one question remains: Does it actually want to govern?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: At least 3 students killed in school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65301b2acf36cae5b880ae45ea475a64c4d9982c5c250467414cad7bb1b5b377</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-at-least-3-students-killed-in-school-shooting/a-79319854--78d522a17cea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-at-least-3-students-killed-in-school-shooting/a-79319854?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emergency services received reports of gunfire at the Banga National High School in southern Mindanao on Friday afternoon. At least three students were killed, including the suspected gunman.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Fuel costs dominate debate ahead of polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:487f15b17746b1dbbae1cb4a4d18ad27203cdf0bdc9eab5a32d69a9c6628a747</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-fuel-costs-dominate-debate-ahead-of-polls/live-79324526--187ad46b558c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-fuel-costs-dominate-debate-ahead-of-polls/live-79324526?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's coalition government is grappling with record-high fuel prices ahead of two state elections this weekend. Follow DW for more stories making headlines in Germany.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>High-profile raids spotlight India's food-safety struggles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26037a671b422dba6dd02677385dd8f3eaea0829299bd1e10b9e11a744ea6a5a</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342--7a2317b19494.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent raids at luxury hotels and a wider crackdown on food companies have renewed the debate about food-safety standards and enforcement in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: El Nino leading to driest monsoon in 17 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49050a949c84ddb991db145303fc946d2fcfda189f0b4ab48c4fafdf019a6fef</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-leading-to-driest-monsoon-in-17-years/live-79320496--f47203063b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-leading-to-driest-monsoon-in-17-years/live-79320496?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">El Nino has put India on track for its driest monsoon since 2009. Meanwhile, the Election Commission has barred both Trinamool factions from using the party's name in by-elections. More with DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Protests erupt over deaths of 37 miners in custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be54d70443de95c27e48d2df921e90adb910f29c0985df520a629412dcf4d5e2</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-protests-erupt-over-deaths-of-37-miners-in-custody/a-79316847--075eb6c61d78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-protests-erupt-over-deaths-of-37-miners-in-custody/a-79316847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of suspects accused of illegal mining were found dead in custody in Nigeria's north-central Niger State. Officials blame disease, while reports cite overcrowding and poor ventilation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9755d39710fc28bf53e48f48d6e8b707f1d8c1b337d052ef9cd95046356342d7</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ea10f43316743f98511babd761d8e3d4895445a968d33513bb342b953aa6ac</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c8ac6e21a14196946084ac027ac1ab556095261f5e2cb3d72402cef5a61a7ec</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e0298b1f33e7ad2dbb604d79367a5bb28c2e082cde2b3da1e3bf3808b648f8</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Organized crime and drug-related deaths rise Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38b975413ff131f5a13f21af2b9462ebb480336be95a732c922f8fb7497ae1a9</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/organized-crime-and-drug-related-deaths-rise-germany/a-79315774--74932d6d2d5d.html" type="text/html"