></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37de42eb13ff2f9ef2c68ba41b09026b6b10842cd38821edaf29830b6ffcc07c</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden environmental cost of AI data centers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fef6864c1f0a05a5dd72da998d06b902feb61765169271ccf7eb4684c09d97a7</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889--5e00024ffa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As data centers multiply to meet AI demand, they're straining power grids, draining water supplies and reshaping the land and air around them.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:872c8b5d00b2883870a4f9e7dcc4c26e02b62b9b132fcaffb805a36066841918</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--acfa7a18352e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https: