ew Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fe1ba89416464a3c8a5fee6a96138a03a77bdacf3e3ecf8159efc2a3c84e152</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--ec9f6d3fb1f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>At Venice Film Festival, politics take center stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b2c38a7f403256d937c936e55bfd6261524f3050b781401cc31f72257a315cd</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761--39adfe1f0702.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With works about Gaza, Ukraine and Elon Musk, political cinema is in the spotlight at the 2026 Venice Film Festival.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney holds firm against Trump tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab3dec435c782dffaaadc6b20a89f5d0253fb8e149f04ac3038af37578a386f4</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754--4ad6d16c6985.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada is facing new US import penalties after Prime Minister Mark Carney refused to match US tariffs on China. Other countries are watching as the Trump trade clash turns into a fight over economic sovereignty.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Inside the sea cucumber smuggling boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:324f0d971671a0d4358c4611b540b98a796387acf894ae3a3fe69b7a188a5f53</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662--ad829420fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quiet multimillion‑dollar black market is exploding across the Indian Ocean, driven by one unlikely animal: the sea cucumber.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ailing Djokovic 'despised' every moment of US Open defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffba8d841f61d58a2b66fa9d2d28f6a91344f8fae5ba4dbf5dcfb33eb9ba77a1</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187--352c93994800.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Novak Djokovic has exited in the first round of a Grand Slam for the first time in over two decades. Could time — or an unknown health condition — be catching up with the Serbian tennis legend?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU wants drones to spray pesticides, but it could backfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fc9548ff55a8484c2094c617d5311d197e114a0e1f895568ab44246ecb68dbb</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154--b8aa3ba6b326.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to lift a decades-old ban on spraying pesticides from the air, allowing drones to be used for greater precision. But experts warn the plan could lead to even more pesticides being used in agriculture.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:965f8afb050fe3a052954d20be25e6b6e7b3c1a33d119f7ac220bef9fde1e79f</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What 'The Odyssey' can teach us about climate chaos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a854814ea7d83b7511e8864f8880737aa446cb278e68248cb2f594a48eb5489</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-odyssey-can-teach-us-about-climate-chaos/a-78545407--d5adc3479f14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-odyssey-can-teach-us-about-climate-chaos/a-78545407?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bronze Age collapse may have started with a water crisis. The droughts of today raise the unsettling question of whether it could happen again.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Influential humanists: These are the winners of the Goethe Medal 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1780b337c606ef40a09545195e3074d853388e2c18b53b9be9bc6062467d3ad8</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975--2a003f94b40a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The prestigious German cultural award recognizes the artistic work and commitment to cultural dialogue of Arvo Pärt, Anita Raja and Prodromos Tsinikoris.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1868aa9be3c34c82ca316049878b27047ed85659cff03a803998ad1b2f0940af</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--a4ab0409cda1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Thieves steal Bronze Age gold in lightning raid on Villena Museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf4839d8c5ecc0f96b0018cb25340753f1aabacee860c096c5afc06a3c08c52d</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T19:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-thieves-steal-bronze-age-gold-in-lightning-raid-on-villena-museum/a-78538027--71179a9fbd6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-thieves-steal-bronze-age-gold-in-lightning-raid-on-villena-museum/a-78538027?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of the world's greatest Bronze Age gold collections has been swiped, almost in its entirety, from Villena Museum. A highly professional group of thieves were in and out in four minutes flat before the museum opened.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tragedy in Nepal: How do flash floods happen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d345a9719468c1c00e9af17b44089c342194e2d7a295da142ba3b9384f4d5801</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421--1b448fe4e3c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When flash floods sweep through the Himalayas, there is often little time to react. Scientists are working to understand the risks and improve early warning systems.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Andre Rankel named Germany's new men's ice hockey coach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93bbbadb50f0f6cb80470a066f4584f867f9939481d695bab3543f64c0eaf5e3</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470--9672475007d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's men's ice hockey team has appointed a new head coach following a string of dissappointing tournaments. He's two decades younger than the man he's replacing but he has no previous experience as a head coach.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>New study shows German football remains male-dominated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5638d23fcd02ab4461f7b151a4758f2bdc66e36563d597d41963035c6bf267b</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569--b9ee319bf21e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The top leagues of German football remain a largely male environment. A new study reveals that only seven clubs have women in upper management levels.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Venus' US Open invitation raises questions about wild cards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:deb2508323879902f3e6beed31182792205eb1fbe51611eb275d56014b8bfbfd</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venus-us-open-invitation-raises-questions-about-wild-cards/a-78524056--49b415adc5c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venus-us-open-invitation-raises-questions-about-wild-cards/a-78524056?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although her current world ranking wouldn't allow it, Venus Williams is set to play singles in the US Open – thanks to a wild card. Who gets these coveted spots—and how?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The great lake divide: Collapse vs. comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afe654dc6891de436848c0f728c515da0fedabccc383668abc6984c5e2097fd9</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263--04bbfa728d70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of the world's biggest lakes vanish in real time, others are proving that recovery is still within reach.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Why social media addiction is so hard to regulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:334c75cda323af3af88b2013735a28a4aa2ff0eeccd07d72b8fbd503b3a01010</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-social-media-addiction-is-so-hard-to-regulate/a-78482023--933d64d6576a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-social-media-addiction-is-so-hard-to-regulate/a-78482023?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facebook, Instagram and other social media platforms are accused of deliberately fostering addictive behavior among young users. Yet regulators continue to struggle to rein in their engagement-driven business models.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama dies at 97</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:532a4beca60ceaaa76b9bf34c2892166f9b0ede3e7a7a11505c450228750dc33</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T02:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japanese-artist-yayoi-kusama-dies-at-97/a-78518473--ef335263e2f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japanese-artist-yayoi-kusama-dies-at-97/a-78518473?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From works of "self-obliteration" to polka dotted nudes, the pioneering artist developed a unique body of work likely to be relevant for years to come.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Was the heat of this summer really 'normal?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27ac34d2fa73b08ff196585398e8351d9b41b01a9bd75af436dfee943430a9fa</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/was-the-heat-of-this-summer-really-normal/a-78513682--d3f656ecebd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/was-the-heat-of-this-summer-really-normal/a-78513682?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some political messaging denies the role of human-caused climate change in this summer's extreme heat. The science tells a different story.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Tim Curry, of 'The Rocky Horror Picture Show,' dies at 80</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb5ab186676d413db75cf62c4ddfecd13c6ba46ceed030a663526ff2ea2e5f95</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T16:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tim-curry-of-the-rocky-horror-picture-show-dies-at-80/a-78514945--42aea1d6e079.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tim-curry-of-the-rocky-horror-picture-show-dies-at-80/a-78514945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The gender-bending role as Dr. Frank-N-Furter put Curry on the map in 1975. He then went on to play a number of villainous roles like Gomez Addams, Pennywise and Bill Sikes, but also Mozart and William Shakespeare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gamescom 2026: What's next for the gaming industry?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a73a09e4ed61d8f76b4401bd29b37834c9f47e8611d6a914a7abcee005c7fdce</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849--a4d043f1bdf6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Gamescom 2026 opens in Cologne, AI, hardware costs and slowing user growth are putting pressure on the global games industry despite its current strength.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's Volkswagen could cut 100,000 jobs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca061e0d8c09a9e09a26c0b40f89f20f2c0a4877775f439f5cb54328d81dab0b</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715--3ad4df2f83bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe's biggest automaker, Volkswagen, faces Chinese competition, high costs and US tariffs. What could its restructuring mean for the German car industry?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can new US sanctions cripple Iran's shadow economy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9a8fe826fc79c12b1e1df6a3e66a2faead6e4dbc023562f4a29137b7eacdb2</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630--d793d396bd52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is expanding sanctions on Iran's financial networks, targeting crypto, gold, aviation and shipping. DW spoke with analysts about what could change.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trees are vital for cooler cities, but they need help too</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80d5194fcf3ee9db81a59a603f0212971be4b2c49655a014a424df07eff6a34e</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trees-are-vital-for-cooler-cities-but-they-need-help-too/a-78488665--39588bf2d5df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trees-are-vital-for-cooler-cities-but-they-need-help-too/a-78488665?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record-breaking heat and drought are putting urban trees at risk. Experts explain how to protect these essential assets and build city forests that can withstand the climate challenges ahead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Scientists discover new 'immune hubs' in skull bone marrow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aad229c1feef2488b411ae99f147337f091e170362bca31abd4c836f68037281</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-new-immune-hubs-in-skull-bone-marrow/a-78460417--3ae7f2c7a79f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-new-immune-hubs-in-skull-bone-marrow/a-78460417?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"Immune hubs" that actively defend the brain have been discovered in mouse skull marrow. Similar cells exist in human skulls, but their role remains unclear.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Spiraling health costs force Iranians to delay care</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dfc2dd7823bb96ad16677f0c3c5caab0f996ff8d81a1b8f1575d7d64d148e65</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430--f9e115d582df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A single chemotherapy session in Iran can cost six times the monthly minimum wage. As drug prices soar and medicine is in short supply, doctors say more patients are delaying or abandoning treatment.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's gas storage levels are so low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:410c329f739cda1dc0ade31dda3f25c3d933915ca3d9dd932402a6c41a77482b</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677--5b5bdc8c00df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage facilities are only 50% full as traders bet that wholesale prices will fall if the Iran war ends. With around three months until winter, DW asks whether the country can refill its reserves in time.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>How Europe can better protect against extreme wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:144b7e0239fd1d7748ef7e2ff91f30350e33b0a91b89c94213d93aebdb74cf6d</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243--a1a3032b9e1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In another summer of European wildfires that have even seen wetlands burning, scientists say the situation is set to worsen in the future. What's needed is fire prevention and climate protection.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
